      "cml:integrityHash": "4d5b762247f363f5fa7d7691ba61d7ae7b9c0481b0a0633e11d1fe845fed16dd",
      "skos:note": "Court may declare a person to be a special witness in relation to the proceeding if satisfied that the person is unlikely to be able to satisfactorily give evidence in the ordinary manner. Definition of vulnerable adult complainant"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-2-sec-19-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "19(1) After section 15YA",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 12,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A vulnerable adult complainant, in relation to a vulnerable adult\nproceeding, is an adult who is, or is alleged to be, a victim of an\noffence, of a kind referred to in subsection 15Y(2), to which the\nproceeding relates."
    },
