    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-19-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "19(1) After section 15YA",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-2-sec-19-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2018c00199.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2018c00199.pdf, p.12",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In a proceeding for a Commonwealth offence, the court may\ndeclare a person to be a special witness in relation to the\nproceeding if satisfied that the person is unlikely to be able to\nsatisfactorily give evidence in the ordinary manner because of:\n\n(a) a disability; or\n\nSupporting victims and witnesses in criminal proceedings  Schedule 2\nVulnerable witness protections  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Law Enforcement Integrity, Vulnerable Witness\nProtection and Other Measures) Act 2013\nCompilation date: 23/5/18\nRegistered: 30/5/18\n\n(b) intimidation, distress or emotional trauma arising from:\n\n(i) the person’s age, cultural background or relationship to\na party to the proceeding; or\n\n(ii) the nature of the evidence; or\n\n(iii) some other relevant factor.\nNote:\nSuch a declaration can also be made in a related proceeding (see\nsubsection 15Y(5)).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In a proceeding for a Commonwealth offence, the court may\ndeclare a person to be a special witness in relation to the\nproceeding if satisfied that the person is unlikely to be able to\nsatisfactorily give evidence in the ordinary manner because of:\n\n(a) a disability; or\n\nSupporting victims and witnesses in criminal proceedings  Schedule 2\nVulnerable witness protections  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Law Enforcement Integrity, Vulnerable Witness\nProtection and Other Measures) Act 2013\nCompilation date: 23/5/18\nRegistered: 30/5/18\n\n(b) intimidation, distress or emotional trauma arising from:\n\n(i) the person’s age, cultural background or relationship to\na party to the proceeding; or\n\n(ii) the nature of the evidence; or\n\n(iii) some other relevant factor.\nNote:\nSuch a declaration can also be made in a related proceeding (see\nsubsection 15Y(5)).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-19"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-19-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-19-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-19-ss-1-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-19-ss-1-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-19-ss-1-logic-alleninterval-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-19-ss-1-logic-ltl-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-19-ss-1-logic-diffusion-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-19-ss-1-logic-argumentation-7"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a716c56c919768f53df53fcb1b3af2a42dc9c44e69a27efbdc4797555eb0cba0",
      "skos:note": "Court may declare a person to be a special witness in relation to the proceeding if satisfied that the person is unlikely to be able to satisfactorily give evidence in the ordinary manner. Definition of vulnerable adult complainant"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-2-sec-19-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "19(1) After section 15YA",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 12,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In a proceeding for a Commonwealth offence, the court may\ndeclare a person to be a special witness in relation to the\nproceeding if satisfied that the person is unlikely to be able to\nsatisfactorily give evidence in the ordinary manner because of:\n\n(a) a disability; or\n\nSupporting victims and witnesses in criminal proceedings  Schedule 2\nVulnerable witness protections  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Law Enforcement Integrity, Vulnerable Witness\nProtection and Other Measures) Act 2013\nCompilation date: 23/5/18\nRegistered: 30/5/18\n\n(b) intimidation, distress or emotional trauma arising from:\n\n(i) the person’s age, cultural background or relationship to\na party to the proceeding; or\n\n(ii) the nature of the evidence; or\n\n(iii) some other relevant factor.\nNote:\nSuch a declaration can also be made in a related proceeding (see\nsubsection 15Y(5))."
    },
