    {
      "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-279",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "279 1  Proceedings to which this Division applies",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-2-sec-279"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2018c00199.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2018c00199.pdf, p.25",
      "values:originalText": "This Division applies to a proceeding for an offence against any of\nthe following Divisions of this Chapter:\n\n(a) Division 270 (slavery and slavery-like conditions);\n\n(b) Division 271 (trafficking in persons and debt bondage);\n\n(c) Division 272 (child sex offences outside Australia);\n\n(d) Division 273 (offences involving child pornography material\nor child abuse material outside Australia).",
      "skos:definition": "This Division applies to a proceeding for an offence against any of\nthe following Divisions of this Chapter:\n\n(a) Division 270 (slavery and slavery-like conditions);\n\n(b) Division 271 (trafficking in persons and debt bondage);\n\n(c) Division 272 (child sex offences outside Australia);\n\n(d) Division 273 (offences involving child pornography material\nor child abuse material outside Australia).",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-279-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-279-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "10f02145becd1ee5fb5cbedcbd184ca24ba36a70c3e6eb9562901b3a2d4dcfaa",
      "skos:note": "Proceedings for an offence against certain Divisions of this Chapter apply to this Division."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-2-sec-279",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "279 1  Proceedings to which this Division applies",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 25,
      "values:originalText": "This Division applies to a proceeding for an offence against any of\nthe following Divisions of this Chapter:\n\n(a) Division 270 (slavery and slavery-like conditions);\n\n(b) Division 271 (trafficking in persons and debt bondage);\n\n(c) Division 272 (child sex offences outside Australia);\n\n(d) Division 273 (offences involving child pornography material\nor child abuse material outside Australia)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-279-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-279"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-279-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "applies",
      "cml:logicSummary": "This Division applies to the specified proceedings.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-279-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "279 2  When court may take evidence by video link",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-2-sec-279-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2018c00199.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2018c00199.pdf, p.25",
      "values:originalText": "In a proceeding, the court may, on application by a party to the\nproceeding, direct that a witness give evidence by video link if:\n\n(a) the witness will give the evidence from outside Australia; and\n\n(b) the witness is not a defendant in the proceeding; and\n\n(c) the facilities required by section 279.3 are available or can\nreasonably be made available; and\n\n(d) the court is satisfied that attendance of the witness at the\ncourt to give the evidence would:\n\nSchedule 2  Supporting victims and witnesses in criminal proceedings",
      "skos:definition": "In a proceeding, the court may, on application by a party to the\nproceeding, direct that a witness give evidence by video link if:\n\n(a) the witness will give the evidence from outside Australia; and\n\n(b) the witness is not a defendant in the proceeding; and\n\n(c) the facilities required by section 279.3 are available or can\nreasonably be made available; and\n\n(d) the court is satisfied that attendance of the witness at the\ncourt to give the evidence would:\n\nSchedule 2  Supporting victims and witnesses in criminal proceedings",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-279-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-279-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f0c34dfe9740ec585f5304f4a5fca8c75cc89f7f4a9f9f7e4935c091b127fae9",
      "skos:note": "Court may direct witness give evidence by video link under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-2-sec-279-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "279 2  When court may take evidence by video link",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 25,
      "values:originalText": "In a proceeding, the court may, on application by a party to the\nproceeding, direct that a witness give evidence by video link if:\n\n(a) the witness will give the evidence from outside Australia; and\n\n(b) the witness is not a defendant in the proceeding; and\n\n(c) the facilities required by section 279.3 are available or can\nreasonably be made available; and\n\n(d) the court is satisfied that attendance of the witness at the\ncourt to give the evidence would:\n\nSchedule 2  Supporting victims and witnesses in criminal proceedings"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-279-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-279-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-279-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Permit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Court permits witness to give evidence by video link.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "None",
      "cml:conclusionText": "None"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-279-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "279 3  Technical requirements for video link",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-2-sec-279-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2018c00199.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2018c00199.pdf, p.26",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A witness can give evidence under a direction only if:\n\n(a) the courtroom or other place in Australia where the court is\nsitting (the Australian location); and\n\n(b) the place where the evidence is given (the overseas location);\nare equipped with video facilities that:\n\n(c) enable appropriate persons at the Australian location to see\nand hear the witness give the evidence; and\n\n(d) enable appropriate persons at the overseas location to see and\nhear appropriate persons at the Australian location.\n\n(2) In subsection (1):\nappropriate persons means such persons as the court considers\nappropriate.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A witness can give evidence under a direction only if:\n\n(a) the courtroom or other place in Australia where the court is\nsitting (the Australian location); and\n\n(b) the place where the evidence is given (the overseas location);\nare equipped with video facilities that:\n\n(c) enable appropriate persons at the Australian location to see\nand hear the witness give the evidence; and\n\n(d) enable appropriate persons at the overseas location to see and\nhear appropriate persons at the Australian location.\n\n(2) In subsection (1):\nappropriate persons means such persons as the court considers\nappropriate.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-279-3-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-279-3-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "092d44c60dc2f6d02dd133312052e9a9cc344a34360ec4589307af91bedcf927"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-2-sec-279-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "279 3  Technical requirements for video link",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 26,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A witness can give evidence under a direction only if:\n\n(a) the courtroom or other place in Australia where the court is\nsitting (the Australian location); and\n\n(b) the place where the evidence is given (the overseas location);\nare equipped with video facilities that:\n\n(c) enable appropriate persons at the Australian location to see\nand hear the witness give the evidence; and\n\n(d) enable appropriate persons at the overseas location to see and\nhear appropriate persons at the Australian location.\n\n(2) In subsection (1):\nappropriate persons means such persons as the court considers\nappropriate."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-279-3-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "279(1) 3  Technical requirements for video link",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-2-sec-279-3-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
