    {
      "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-16ab-ss-7",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "16AB(7) Matters relating to victim impact statements",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-2-sec-16ab-ss-7"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2018c00199.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2018c00199.pdf, p.30",
      "values:originalText": "(7) For the purposes of Part IAD (about protecting vulnerable\npersons):\n\n(a) giving evidence includes giving a reading under\nsubsection (4); and\n\n(b) a cross-examination includes a cross-examination under\nsubsection (6).\nNote:\nThis confirms that any protections available under Part IAD will be\navailable for the reading or the cross-examination.\n\nSupporting victims and witnesses in criminal proceedings  Schedule 2\nApplication of amendments  Part 3\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Law Enforcement Integrity, Vulnerable Witness\nProtection and Other Measures) Act 2013\nCompilation date: 23/5/18\nRegistered: 30/5/18",
      "skos:definition": "(7) For the purposes of Part IAD (about protecting vulnerable\npersons):\n\n(a) giving evidence includes giving a reading under\nsubsection (4); and\n\n(b) a cross-examination includes a cross-examination under\nsubsection (6).\nNote:\nThis confirms that any protections available under Part IAD will be\navailable for the reading or the cross-examination.\n\nSupporting victims and witnesses in criminal proceedings  Schedule 2\nApplication of amendments  Part 3\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Law Enforcement Integrity, Vulnerable Witness\nProtection and Other Measures) Act 2013\nCompilation date: 23/5/18\nRegistered: 30/5/18",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-16ab"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-16ab-ss-7-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-16ab-ss-7-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-2-sec-16ab-ss-7-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "aa144f7fe0edc3f2576c33bfb46ab08fcffe55e8dd1001702569bac2bb43a3e1",
      "skos:note": "Parties to criminal proceedings must provide a reading or cross-examination under specific subsections.",
      "dc:description": "True"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-2-sec-16ab-ss-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "16AB(7) Matters relating to victim impact statements",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 30,
      "values:originalText": "(7) For the purposes of Part IAD (about protecting vulnerable\npersons):\n\n(a) giving evidence includes giving a reading under\nsubsection (4); and\n\n(b) a cross-examination includes a cross-examination under\nsubsection (6).\nNote:\nThis confirms that any protections available under Part IAD will be\navailable for the reading or the cross-examination.\n\nSupporting victims and witnesses in criminal proceedings  Schedule 2\nApplication of amendments  Part 3\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Law Enforcement Integrity, Vulnerable Witness\nProtection and Other Measures) Act 2013\nCompilation date: 23/5/18\nRegistered: 30/5/18"
    },
