      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3 Section 236A",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 32,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the section, substitute:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-3-sec-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-3-sec-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-3-sec-236a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "236A No discharge without conviction for certain offences",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-3-sec-236a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2018c00199.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2018c00199.pdf, p.32",
      "values:originalText": "The court may only make an order under section 19B of the Crimes\nAct 1914 (discharge of offenders without conviction) in respect of\na charge for an offence against section 233B, 233C or 234A if the\nperson charged was aged under 18 when the offence was alleged to\nhave been committed.\nNote:\nSee also section 236D, which relates to age.",
      "skos:definition": "The court may only make an order under section 19B of the Crimes\nAct 1914 (discharge of offenders without conviction) in respect of\na charge for an offence against section 233B, 233C or 234A if the\nperson charged was aged under 18 when the offence was alleged to\nhave been committed.\nNote:\nSee also section 236D, which relates to age.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-3-sec-236a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-3-sec-236a-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ce6dde531933fd70048efc6d37916e91f6559fc1f7ea9bb732ba5fb7695f1d90",
      "skos:note": "Court may only make order for certain offence under specific conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-3-sec-236a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "236A No discharge without conviction for certain offences",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 32,
      "values:originalText": "The court may only make an order under section 19B of the Crimes\nAct 1914 (discharge of offenders without conviction) in respect of\na charge for an offence against section 233B, 233C or 234A if the\nperson charged was aged under 18 when the offence was alleged to\nhave been committed.\nNote:\nSee also section 236D, which relates to age."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-3-sec-236a-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-3-sec-236a"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-3-sec-236a-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "only",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Restricts court action to specific circumstances.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-3-sec-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 At the end of Subdivision A of Division 12 of Part 2",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-3-sec-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2018c00199.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2018c00199.pdf, p.32",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\nDeterring people smuggling  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Law Enforcement Integrity, Vulnerable Witness\nProtection and Other Measures) Act 2013\nCompilation date: 23/5/18\nRegistered: 30/5/18\n\n236C  Time in immigration detention counts for sentencing etc.\n\n(1) This section applies to the court when imposing a sentence on, or\nsetting a non-parole period for, a person convicted of an offence\nagainst this Subdivision.\n\n(2) The court must take into account any period that the person has\nspent in immigration detention during the period:\n\n(a) starting when the offence was committed; and\n\n(b) ending when the person is sentenced for the offence.\nNote:\nThis enables the court to take into account time spent while not in\npunitive detention.\n\n(3) Neither section 236B nor this section prevents section 16E of the\nCrimes Act 1914 from applying to the imposition of the sentence or\nthe setting of the non-parole period.\nNote:\nSection 16E of the Crimes Act 1914 applies State law to aspects of\nsentencing for federal offences, subject to specified exceptions.",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\n\nDeterring people smuggling  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Law Enforcement Integrity, Vulnerable Witness\nProtection and Other Measures) Act 2013\nCompilation date: 23/5/18\nRegistered: 30/5/18\n\n236C  Time in immigration detention counts for sentencing etc.\n\n(1) This section applies to the court when imposing a sentence on, or\nsetting a non-parole period for, a person convicted of an offence\nagainst this Subdivision.\n\n(2) The court must take into account any period that the person has\nspent in immigration detention during the period:\n\n(a) starting when the offence was committed; and\n\n(b) ending when the person is sentenced for the offence.\nNote:\nThis enables the court to take into account time spent while not in\npunitive detention.\n\n(3) Neither section 236B nor this section prevents section 16E of the\nCrimes Act 1914 from applying to the imposition of the sentence or\nthe setting of the non-parole period.\nNote:\nSection 16E of the Crimes Act 1914 applies State law to aspects of\nsentencing for federal offences, subject to specified exceptions.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-3-sec-4-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-3-sec-4-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-3-sec-4-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "41db9532d403f20055bc57e0cbe059d8dfc5662e00a4dc3cc21d0603d25bed8d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-3-sec-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 At the end of Subdivision A of Division 12 of Part 2",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 32,
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\nDeterring people smuggling  Schedule 3\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Law Enforcement Integrity, Vulnerable Witness\nProtection and Other Measures) Act 2013\nCompilation date: 23/5/18\nRegistered: 30/5/18\n\n236C  Time in immigration detention counts for sentencing etc.\n\n(1) This section applies to the court when imposing a sentence on, or\nsetting a non-parole period for, a person convicted of an offence\nagainst this Subdivision.\n\n(2) The court must take into account any period that the person has\nspent in immigration detention during the period:\n\n(a) starting when the offence was committed; and\n\n(b) ending when the person is sentenced for the offence.\nNote:\nThis enables the court to take into account time spent while not in\npunitive detention.\n\n(3) Neither section 236B nor this section prevents section 16E of the\nCrimes Act 1914 from applying to the imposition of the sentence or\nthe setting of the non-parole period.\nNote:\nSection 16E of the Crimes Act 1914 applies State law to aspects of\nsentencing for federal offences, subject to specified exceptions."
    },
