      "dc:source": "c2018c00199.pdf, p.32",
      "values:originalText": "(3) Neither section 236B nor this section prevents section 16E of the\nCrimes Act 1914 from applying to the imposition of the sentence or\nthe setting of the non-parole period.\nNote:\nSection 16E of the Crimes Act 1914 applies State law to aspects of\nsentencing for federal offences, subject to specified exceptions.",
