      "cml:premiseText": "A written certificate may be issued under this subsection",
      "cml:conclusionText": "by the specified individuals"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-3-sec-236f",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "236F Evidentiary certificates—procedural matters",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-3-sec-236f"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2018c00199.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2018c00199.pdf, p.35",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A certificate issued under subsection 236E(1) must not be admitted\nin evidence in proceedings for an offence unless:\n\n(a) the person charged with the offence; or\n\n(b) a lawyer who has appeared for the person in those\nproceedings;\nhas, at least 28 days before the certificate is sought to be so\nadmitted, been given a copy of the certificate together with notice\nof the intention to produce the certificate as evidence in the\nproceedings.\n\n(2) If, under section 236E, a certificate is admitted in evidence in\nproceedings for an offence, the person charged with the offence\nmay require the person who signed the certificate to be:\n\n(a) called as a witness for the prosecution; and\n\nSchedule 3  Deterring people smuggling",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A certificate issued under subsection 236E(1) must not be admitted\nin evidence in proceedings for an offence unless:\n\n(a) the person charged with the offence; or\n\n(b) a lawyer who has appeared for the person in those\nproceedings;\nhas, at least 28 days before the certificate is sought to be so\nadmitted, been given a copy of the certificate together with notice\nof the intention to produce the certificate as evidence in the\nproceedings.\n\n(2) If, under section 236E, a certificate is admitted in evidence in\nproceedings for an offence, the person charged with the offence\nmay require the person who signed the certificate to be:\n\n(a) called as a witness for the prosecution; and\n\nSchedule 3  Deterring people smuggling",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-3-sec-236f-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-3-sec-236f-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "924a345ec662d30927cea97a950677a855cddc697c59ddc3e3c3ab59713a79ff"
    },
    {
