    {
      "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-3-sec-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5 Application of amendments",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-3-sec-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2018c00199.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2018c00199.pdf, p.36",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe amendment made by item 3 applies in relation to offences\ncommitted (or alleged to have been committed) at or after the\ncommencement of this Part.\n(2)\nSection 236C (about time in immigration detention) of the Migration\nAct 1958 (as inserted by this Part) applies in relation to sentences\nimposed, or non-parole periods set, at or after the commencement of\nthis Part (whether the relevant offence was committed before, at or after\nthat commencement).\n(3)\nSection 236D (about burden and standard of proof in relation to age) of\nthe Migration Act 1958 (as inserted by this Part) applies in relation to\nclaims made, at or after the commencement of this Part, by defendants\nin proceedings (whether the proceedings began before, at or after that\ncommencement).\n(4)\nSections 236E and 236F (about evidentiary certificates) of the\nMigration Act 1958 (as inserted by this Part) apply in relation to the\nboarding of ships or aircraft, or the chasing of ships not boarded, at or\nafter the commencement of this Part.\n\nDeterring people smuggling  Schedule 3\nOther amendments  Part 2\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Law Enforcement Integrity, Vulnerable Witness\nProtection and Other Measures) Act 2013\nCompilation date: 23/5/18\nRegistered: 30/5/18",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nThe amendment made by item 3 applies in relation to offences\ncommitted (or alleged to have been committed) at or after the\ncommencement of this Part.\n(2)\nSection 236C (about time in immigration detention) of the Migration\nAct 1958 (as inserted by this Part) applies in relation to sentences\nimposed, or non-parole periods set, at or after the commencement of\nthis Part (whether the relevant offence was committed before, at or after\nthat commencement).\n(3)\nSection 236D (about burden and standard of proof in relation to age) of\nthe Migration Act 1958 (as inserted by this Part) applies in relation to\nclaims made, at or after the commencement of this Part, by defendants\nin proceedings (whether the proceedings began before, at or after that\ncommencement).\n(4)\nSections 236E and 236F (about evidentiary certificates) of the\nMigration Act 1958 (as inserted by this Part) apply in relation to the\nboarding of ships or aircraft, or the chasing of ships not boarded, at or\nafter the commencement of this Part.\n\nDeterring people smuggling  Schedule 3\nOther amendments  Part 2\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Law Enforcement Integrity, Vulnerable Witness\nProtection and Other Measures) Act 2013\nCompilation date: 23/5/18\nRegistered: 30/5/18",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-3-sec-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-3-sec-5-logic-alleninterval-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-3-sec-5-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-3-sec-5-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-3-sec-5-logic-alleninterval-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "eca607dbcb4f20f14c3d1a5753690ea286bef66768094224895363eba090cabf",
      "skos:note": "Application of amendments"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-3-sec-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5 Application of amendments",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 36,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe amendment made by item 3 applies in relation to offences\ncommitted (or alleged to have been committed) at or after the\ncommencement of this Part.\n(2)\nSection 236C (about time in immigration detention) of the Migration\nAct 1958 (as inserted by this Part) applies in relation to sentences\nimposed, or non-parole periods set, at or after the commencement of\nthis Part (whether the relevant offence was committed before, at or after\nthat commencement).\n(3)\nSection 236D (about burden and standard of proof in relation to age) of\nthe Migration Act 1958 (as inserted by this Part) applies in relation to\nclaims made, at or after the commencement of this Part, by defendants\nin proceedings (whether the proceedings began before, at or after that\ncommencement).\n(4)\nSections 236E and 236F (about evidentiary certificates) of the\nMigration Act 1958 (as inserted by this Part) apply in relation to the\nboarding of ships or aircraft, or the chasing of ships not boarded, at or\nafter the commencement of this Part.\n\nDeterring people smuggling  Schedule 3\nOther amendments  Part 2\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Law Enforcement Integrity, Vulnerable Witness\nProtection and Other Measures) Act 2013\nCompilation date: 23/5/18\nRegistered: 30/5/18"
    },
    {
