    {
      "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-3-sec-10",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10 Application and transitional provisions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-3-sec-10"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2018c00199.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2018c00199.pdf, p.38",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe amendments made by this Part apply in relation to authorisations\nmade at or after the commencement of this Part.\n(2)\nThe amendments made by this Part do not apply in relation to the\ncontinuous exercise of powers (within the meaning of the Maritime\nPowers Act 2013) begun under the Migration Act 1958 before the\ncommencement of this Part.\nNote:\nAfter that commencement, an evidentiary certificate may be issued under section 236E\nof the Migration Act 1958 (as in force before that commencement) in relation to a\nboarding, or chase, begun under Division 12A of Part 2 of that Act before that\ncommencement.\n\nAnti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing amendments  Schedule 4\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Law Enforcement Integrity, Vulnerable Witness\nProtection and Other Measures) Act 2013\nCompilation date: 23/5/18\nRegistered: 30/5/18",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nThe amendments made by this Part apply in relation to authorisations\nmade at or after the commencement of this Part.\n(2)\nThe amendments made by this Part do not apply in relation to the\ncontinuous exercise of powers (within the meaning of the Maritime\nPowers Act 2013) begun under the Migration Act 1958 before the\ncommencement of this Part.\nNote:\nAfter that commencement, an evidentiary certificate may be issued under section 236E\nof the Migration Act 1958 (as in force before that commencement) in relation to a\nboarding, or chase, begun under Division 12A of Part 2 of that Act before that\ncommencement.\n\nAnti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing amendments  Schedule 4\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Law Enforcement Integrity, Vulnerable Witness\nProtection and Other Measures) Act 2013\nCompilation date: 23/5/18\nRegistered: 30/5/18",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-3-sec-10-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-3-sec-10-logic-alleninterval-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4932e3079d4f9b34fc687edf2b9f6cd9e4074df6d67971f3da9bdae13b2a7f48",
      "skos:note": "Amendments apply in relation to authorisations made at or after commencement, but not continuous exercise of powers begun before commencement."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-3-sec-10",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10 Application and transitional provisions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 38,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nThe amendments made by this Part apply in relation to authorisations\nmade at or after the commencement of this Part.\n(2)\nThe amendments made by this Part do not apply in relation to the\ncontinuous exercise of powers (within the meaning of the Maritime\nPowers Act 2013) begun under the Migration Act 1958 before the\ncommencement of this Part.\nNote:\nAfter that commencement, an evidentiary certificate may be issued under section 236E\nof the Migration Act 1958 (as in force before that commencement) in relation to a\nboarding, or chase, begun under Division 12A of Part 2 of that Act before that\ncommencement.\n\nAnti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing amendments  Schedule 4\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Law Enforcement Integrity, Vulnerable Witness\nProtection and Other Measures) Act 2013\nCompilation date: 23/5/18\nRegistered: 30/5/18"
    },
    {
