    {
      "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-233a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "233A Simplified outline",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-4-sec-233a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2018c00199.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2018c00199.pdf, p.44",
      "values:originalText": "The following is a simplified outline of this Part:\n•\nCertain decisions of delegates of the AUSTRAC CEO may be\nreviewed by the Administrative Appeals Tribunal following a\nprocess of internal reconsideration by the AUSTRAC CEO.\n•\nCertain decisions of the AUSTRAC CEO may be reviewed by\nthe Administrative Appeals Tribunal.",
      "skos:definition": "The following is a simplified outline of this Part:\n•\nCertain decisions of delegates of the AUSTRAC CEO may be\nreviewed by the Administrative Appeals Tribunal following a\nprocess of internal reconsideration by the AUSTRAC CEO.\n•\nCertain decisions of the AUSTRAC CEO may be reviewed by\nthe Administrative Appeals Tribunal.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-233a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-233a-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5650fa569da5ada7f797314f504eacb6b32aee940a060c6c173fac193b98aea0",
      "skos:note": "Review of AUSTRAC CEO decisions by Administrative Appeals Tribunal"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-4-sec-233a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "233A Simplified outline",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 44,
      "values:originalText": "The following is a simplified outline of this Part:\n•\nCertain decisions of delegates of the AUSTRAC CEO may be\nreviewed by the Administrative Appeals Tribunal following a\nprocess of internal reconsideration by the AUSTRAC CEO.\n•\nCertain decisions of the AUSTRAC CEO may be reviewed by\nthe Administrative Appeals Tribunal."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-233a-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-233a"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-233a-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "may be reviewed",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Review obligation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "AUSTRAC CEO decision",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Administrative Appeals Tribunal review"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-233b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "233B Reviewable decisions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-4-sec-233b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2018c00199.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2018c00199.pdf, p.44",
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of this Act, each of the following decisions of the\nAUSTRAC CEO is a reviewable decision:\n\nReviewable decisions\nItem\nDecision\nA decision under subsection 75B(6) or section 75C to refuse to register a\nperson as:\n(a) a remittance network provider; or\n(b) an independent remittance dealer; or\n(c) a remittance affiliate of a registered remittance network provider.\nA decision under section 75E to impose conditions to which a person’s\nregistration is subject.\nA decision under section 75G to cancel a person’s registration.\nA decision under subsection 161(2) to require certain things of a reporting\nentity.\nA decision under subparagraph 161(2)(d)(ii) not to allow a longer period.\nA decision under subsection 191(2) to give a reporting entity a direction.\n\nAnti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing amendments  Schedule 4\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Law Enforcement Integrity, Vulnerable Witness\nProtection and Other Measures) Act 2013\nCompilation date: 23/5/18\nRegistered: 30/5/18",
      "skos:definition": "For the purposes of this Act, each of the following decisions of the\nAUSTRAC CEO is a reviewable decision:\n\nReviewable decisions\nItem\nDecision\nA decision under subsection 75B(6) or section 75C to refuse to register a\nperson as:\n(a) a remittance network provider; or\n(b) an independent remittance dealer; or\n(c) a remittance affiliate of a registered remittance network provider.\nA decision under section 75E to impose conditions to which a person’s\nregistration is subject.\nA decision under section 75G to cancel a person’s registration.\nA decision under subsection 161(2) to require certain things of a reporting\nentity.\nA decision under subparagraph 161(2)(d)(ii) not to allow a longer period.\nA decision under subsection 191(2) to give a reporting entity a direction.\n\nAnti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing amendments  Schedule 4\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Law Enforcement Integrity, Vulnerable Witness\nProtection and Other Measures) Act 2013\nCompilation date: 23/5/18\nRegistered: 30/5/18",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-233b-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-233b-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9171da24e877038a8e0f2308d315452fd6e0b3d4fc020d53e3c0f218c779bd4b",
      "skos:note": "Refusal to register a person as a remittance network provider, independent remittance dealer, or remittance affiliate."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-4-sec-233b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "233B Reviewable decisions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 44,
      "values:originalText": "For the purposes of this Act, each of the following decisions of the\nAUSTRAC CEO is a reviewable decision:\n\nReviewable decisions\nItem\nDecision\nA decision under subsection 75B(6) or section 75C to refuse to register a\nperson as:\n(a) a remittance network provider; or\n(b) an independent remittance dealer; or\n(c) a remittance affiliate of a registered remittance network provider.\nA decision under section 75E to impose conditions to which a person’s\nregistration is subject.\nA decision under section 75G to cancel a person’s registration.\nA decision under subsection 161(2) to require certain things of a reporting\nentity.\nA decision under subparagraph 161(2)(d)(ii) not to allow a longer period.\nA decision under subsection 191(2) to give a reporting entity a direction.\n\nAnti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing amendments  Schedule 4\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Law Enforcement Integrity, Vulnerable Witness\nProtection and Other Measures) Act 2013\nCompilation date: 23/5/18\nRegistered: 30/5/18"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-233b-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-233b"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-233b-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibition of registration",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-233c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "233C Giving notice of reviewable decisions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-4-sec-233c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2018c00199.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2018c00199.pdf, p.45",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The AUSTRAC CEO must, as soon as practicable after a\nreviewable decision is made in relation to one or more persons,\ngive a written notice to each of the persons containing:\n\n(a) the terms of the decision; and\n\n(b) for a decision under section 75G to cancel a person’s\nregistration—the date the cancellation takes effect; and\n\n(c) the reasons for the decision; and\n\n(d) a statement setting out particulars of the persons’ right to\nhave the decision reviewed under this Part.\nNote:\nAn example of a reviewable decision made in relation to 2 persons is a\ndecision refusing to register a person as a remittance affiliate of a\nregistered remittance network provider, if the provider applied under\nsubsection 75B(2) for that person to be so registered.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to reviewable decisions taken to be\nmade because of the operation of subsection 75B(6) (about deemed\nrefusal).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The AUSTRAC CEO must, as soon as practicable after a\nreviewable decision is made in relation to one or more persons,\ngive a written notice to each of the persons containing:\n\n(a) the terms of the decision; and\n\n(b) for a decision under section 75G to cancel a person’s\nregistration—the date the cancellation takes effect; and\n\n(c) the reasons for the decision; and\n\n(d) a statement setting out particulars of the persons’ right to\nhave the decision reviewed under this Part.\nNote:\nAn example of a reviewable decision made in relation to 2 persons is a\ndecision refusing to register a person as a remittance affiliate of a\nregistered remittance network provider, if the provider applied under\nsubsection 75B(2) for that person to be so registered.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to reviewable decisions taken to be\nmade because of the operation of subsection 75B(6) (about deemed\nrefusal).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-233c-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-233c-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "03326942ab74ce581fe611dd5b874efb2fa4d95536a7fe563d2c1e2aaf308e60"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-4-sec-233c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "233C Giving notice of reviewable decisions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 45,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The AUSTRAC CEO must, as soon as practicable after a\nreviewable decision is made in relation to one or more persons,\ngive a written notice to each of the persons containing:\n\n(a) the terms of the decision; and\n\n(b) for a decision under section 75G to cancel a person’s\nregistration—the date the cancellation takes effect; and\n\n(c) the reasons for the decision; and\n\n(d) a statement setting out particulars of the persons’ right to\nhave the decision reviewed under this Part.\nNote:\nAn example of a reviewable decision made in relation to 2 persons is a\ndecision refusing to register a person as a remittance affiliate of a\nregistered remittance network provider, if the provider applied under\nsubsection 75B(2) for that person to be so registered.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to reviewable decisions taken to be\nmade because of the operation of subsection 75B(6) (about deemed\nrefusal)."
    },
