      "skos:definition": "(1) The AUSTRAC CEO must, as soon as practicable after a\nreviewable decision is made in relation to one or more persons,\ngive a written notice to each of the persons containing:\n\n(a) the terms of the decision; and\n\n(b) for a decision under section 75G to cancel a person’s\nregistration—the date the cancellation takes effect; and\n\n(c) the reasons for the decision; and\n\n(d) a statement setting out particulars of the persons’ right to\nhave the decision reviewed under this Part.\nNote:\nAn example of a reviewable decision made in relation to 2 persons is a\ndecision refusing to register a person as a remittance affiliate of a\nregistered remittance network provider, if the provider applied under\nsubsection 75B(2) for that person to be so registered.",
