    {
      "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-233d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "233D Applications for reconsideration of decisions made by",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-4-sec-233d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2018c00199.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2018c00199.pdf, p.45",
      "values:originalText": "delegates of the AUSTRAC CEO\n\n(1) This section applies to a reviewable decision if the decision is\nmade by a delegate of the AUSTRAC CEO.\nNote:\nReviewable decisions made by the AUSTRAC CEO personally may\nbe reviewed by the Administrative Appeals Tribunal (see\nparagraph 233F(b)).\n\n(2) A person affected by a reviewable decision who is dissatisfied with\nthe decision may apply to the AUSTRAC CEO for the decision to\nbe reconsidered.\n\n(3) The application must:\n\n(a) be in the approved form; and\n\n(b) contain the information required by the AML/CTF Rules;\nand\n\n(c) be made within:\n\nSchedule 4  Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing amendments",
      "skos:definition": "delegates of the AUSTRAC CEO\n\n(1) This section applies to a reviewable decision if the decision is\nmade by a delegate of the AUSTRAC CEO.\nNote:\nReviewable decisions made by the AUSTRAC CEO personally may\nbe reviewed by the Administrative Appeals Tribunal (see\nparagraph 233F(b)).\n\n(2) A person affected by a reviewable decision who is dissatisfied with\nthe decision may apply to the AUSTRAC CEO for the decision to\nbe reconsidered.\n\n(3) The application must:\n\n(a) be in the approved form; and\n\n(b) contain the information required by the AML/CTF Rules;\nand\n\n(c) be made within:\n\nSchedule 4  Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing amendments",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-233d-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-233d-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-233d-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e34e9b383b79b01149c1a4ca1f3728bc85f547edca5a3d66836331afa7ff6239"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-4-sec-233d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "233D Applications for reconsideration of decisions made by",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 45,
      "values:originalText": "delegates of the AUSTRAC CEO\n\n(1) This section applies to a reviewable decision if the decision is\nmade by a delegate of the AUSTRAC CEO.\nNote:\nReviewable decisions made by the AUSTRAC CEO personally may\nbe reviewed by the Administrative Appeals Tribunal (see\nparagraph 233F(b)).\n\n(2) A person affected by a reviewable decision who is dissatisfied with\nthe decision may apply to the AUSTRAC CEO for the decision to\nbe reconsidered.\n\n(3) The application must:\n\n(a) be in the approved form; and\n\n(b) contain the information required by the AML/CTF Rules;\nand\n\n(c) be made within:\n\nSchedule 4  Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing amendments"
    },
