    {
      "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-233d-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "233D(3) Applications for reconsideration of decisions made by",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-4-sec-233d-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2018c00199.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2018c00199.pdf, p.45",
      "values:originalText": "(3) The application must:\n\n(a) be in the approved form; and\n\n(b) contain the information required by the AML/CTF Rules;\nand\n\n(c) be made within:\n\nSchedule 4  Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing amendments",
      "skos:definition": "(3) The application must:\n\n(a) be in the approved form; and\n\n(b) contain the information required by the AML/CTF Rules;\nand\n\n(c) be made within:\n\nSchedule 4  Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing amendments",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-233d"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-233d-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-233d-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1ce8b4e1dff70edd5cfbd28529e4bbd40f2640ea9ca657f15d1d4c12402b2275",
      "skos:note": "Application requirements for reconsideration of decisions made by the authority.",
      "dc:description": "Information required by the AML/CTF Rules"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-4-sec-233d-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "233D(3) Applications for reconsideration of decisions made by",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 45,
      "values:originalText": "(3) The application must:\n\n(a) be in the approved form; and\n\n(b) contain the information required by the AML/CTF Rules;\nand\n\n(c) be made within:\n\nSchedule 4  Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing amendments"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-233d-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-233d-ss-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:LegalPerson"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: LegalPerson"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-233d-ss-3-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Application must be made within Schedule 4",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-233e",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "233E Reconsideration of reviewable decisions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-4-sec-233e"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2018c00199.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2018c00199.pdf, p.46",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Upon receiving an application under section 233D, the AUSTRAC\nCEO must reconsider the reviewable decision.\n\n(2) The AUSTRAC CEO must:\n\n(a) affirm, vary or revoke the reviewable decision; and\n\n(b) if the AUSTRAC CEO revokes the reviewable decision,\nmake such other decision (if any) as the AUSTRAC CEO\nthinks appropriate.\n\n(3) The AUSTRAC CEO’s reconsideration must be done by the\nAUSTRAC CEO personally, or by a person to whom the\nAUSTRAC CEO’s power under this section is delegated who:\n\n(a) was not involved in making the reviewable decision; and\n\n(b) occupies a position in AUSTRAC that is senior to that\noccupied by any person involved in making the reviewable\ndecision.\n\n(4) The AUSTRAC CEO must, as soon as practicable after making a\ndecision under subsection (2), give written notice to the applicant\nof:\n\n(a) the decision; and\n\n(b) if the decision is to cancel a person’s registration—the date\nthe cancellation takes effect; and\n\n(c) the reasons for the decision; and\n\n(d) a statement setting out particulars of the applicant’s right to\nhave the decision reviewed by the Administrative Appeals\nTribunal.\n\nAnti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing amendments  Schedule 4\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Law Enforcement Integrity, Vulnerable Witness\nProtection and Other Measures) Act 2013\nCompilation date: 23/5/18\nRegistered: 30/5/18\n\n(5) A decision of the AUSTRAC CEO under subsection (2) has effect\n(except for the purposes of section 233B) as if it were made under\nthe provision under which the reviewable decision was made.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Upon receiving an application under section 233D, the AUSTRAC\nCEO must reconsider the reviewable decision.\n\n(2) The AUSTRAC CEO must:\n\n(a) affirm, vary or revoke the reviewable decision; and\n\n(b) if the AUSTRAC CEO revokes the reviewable decision,\nmake such other decision (if any) as the AUSTRAC CEO\nthinks appropriate.\n\n(3) The AUSTRAC CEO’s reconsideration must be done by the\nAUSTRAC CEO personally, or by a person to whom the\nAUSTRAC CEO’s power under this section is delegated who:\n\n(a) was not involved in making the reviewable decision; and\n\n(b) occupies a position in AUSTRAC that is senior to that\noccupied by any person involved in making the reviewable\ndecision.\n\n(4) The AUSTRAC CEO must, as soon as practicable after making a\ndecision under subsection (2), give written notice to the applicant\nof:\n\n(a) the decision; and\n\n(b) if the decision is to cancel a person’s registration—the date\nthe cancellation takes effect; and\n\n(c) the reasons for the decision; and\n\n(d) a statement setting out particulars of the applicant’s right to\nhave the decision reviewed by the Administrative Appeals\nTribunal.\n\nAnti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing amendments  Schedule 4\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Law Enforcement Integrity, Vulnerable Witness\nProtection and Other Measures) Act 2013\nCompilation date: 23/5/18\nRegistered: 30/5/18\n\n(5) A decision of the AUSTRAC CEO under subsection (2) has effect\n(except for the purposes of section 233B) as if it were made under\nthe provision under which the reviewable decision was made.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-233e-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-233e-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-233e-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-233e-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-233e-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "79c0007a319a44e0f1dad4f962937bbfe89523816f0997bd2a150ec0d6f9e73c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-4-sec-233e",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "233E Reconsideration of reviewable decisions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 46,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Upon receiving an application under section 233D, the AUSTRAC\nCEO must reconsider the reviewable decision.\n\n(2) The AUSTRAC CEO must:\n\n(a) affirm, vary or revoke the reviewable decision; and\n\n(b) if the AUSTRAC CEO revokes the reviewable decision,\nmake such other decision (if any) as the AUSTRAC CEO\nthinks appropriate.\n\n(3) The AUSTRAC CEO’s reconsideration must be done by the\nAUSTRAC CEO personally, or by a person to whom the\nAUSTRAC CEO’s power under this section is delegated who:\n\n(a) was not involved in making the reviewable decision; and\n\n(b) occupies a position in AUSTRAC that is senior to that\noccupied by any person involved in making the reviewable\ndecision.\n\n(4) The AUSTRAC CEO must, as soon as practicable after making a\ndecision under subsection (2), give written notice to the applicant\nof:\n\n(a) the decision; and\n\n(b) if the decision is to cancel a person’s registration—the date\nthe cancellation takes effect; and\n\n(c) the reasons for the decision; and\n\n(d) a statement setting out particulars of the applicant’s right to\nhave the decision reviewed by the Administrative Appeals\nTribunal.\n\nAnti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing amendments  Schedule 4\nMain amendments  Part 1\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Law Enforcement Integrity, Vulnerable Witness\nProtection and Other Measures) Act 2013\nCompilation date: 23/5/18\nRegistered: 30/5/18\n\n(5) A decision of the AUSTRAC CEO under subsection (2) has effect\n(except for the purposes of section 233B) as if it were made under\nthe provision under which the reviewable decision was made."
    },
