    {
      "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-33",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "33 Application and transitional provisions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-4-sec-33"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "c2018c00199.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "c2018c00199.pdf, p.47",
      "values:originalText": "Pending reviews\n(1)\nDespite the repeals and amendments of the Anti-Money Laundering and\nCounter-Terrorism Financing Act 2006 made by this Part, the old law\ncontinues to apply, in relation to each of the following:\n\n(a) a reviewable decision made, or proposed to be made, before\nthe commencement day;\n\n(b) a decision of the AUSTRAC CEO under section 161 or 191\nof that Act made before the commencement day;\nas if those repeals and amendments had not happened.\nNote:\nA consequence of paragraph (a) is that the old law also applies in relation to AAT\nreviewable decisions made after the commencement day in relation to reviewable\ndecisions made, or proposed to be made, before the commencement day.\nSecondary disclosures\n(2)\nSubsections 123(7AA) and (7B), and paragraph 130(3)(a), of the\nAnti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing Act 2006 (as\n\nSchedule 4  Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing amendments",
      "skos:definition": "Pending reviews\n(1)\nDespite the repeals and amendments of the Anti-Money Laundering and\nCounter-Terrorism Financing Act 2006 made by this Part, the old law\ncontinues to apply, in relation to each of the following:\n\n(a) a reviewable decision made, or proposed to be made, before\nthe commencement day;\n\n(b) a decision of the AUSTRAC CEO under section 161 or 191\nof that Act made before the commencement day;\nas if those repeals and amendments had not happened.\nNote:\nA consequence of paragraph (a) is that the old law also applies in relation to AAT\nreviewable decisions made after the commencement day in relation to reviewable\ndecisions made, or proposed to be made, before the commencement day.\nSecondary disclosures\n(2)\nSubsections 123(7AA) and (7B), and paragraph 130(3)(a), of the\nAnti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing Act 2006 (as\n\nSchedule 4  Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing amendments",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-33-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-33-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "22a4e264dcfdbed1e1b64bd1571b749ce9b699c62feb741ef4d21323620136be",
      "skos:note": "Old law continues to apply in relation to certain decisions made before the commencement day."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/c2018c00199#sch-4-sec-33",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "33 Application and transitional provisions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 47,
      "values:originalText": "Pending reviews\n(1)\nDespite the repeals and amendments of the Anti-Money Laundering and\nCounter-Terrorism Financing Act 2006 made by this Part, the old law\ncontinues to apply, in relation to each of the following:\n\n(a) a reviewable decision made, or proposed to be made, before\nthe commencement day;\n\n(b) a decision of the AUSTRAC CEO under section 161 or 191\nof that Act made before the commencement day;\nas if those repeals and amendments had not happened.\nNote:\nA consequence of paragraph (a) is that the old law also applies in relation to AAT\nreviewable decisions made after the commencement day in relation to reviewable\ndecisions made, or proposed to be made, before the commencement day.\nSecondary disclosures\n(2)\nSubsections 123(7AA) and (7B), and paragraph 130(3)(a), of the\nAnti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing Act 2006 (as\n\nSchedule 4  Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing amendments"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-33-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:c2018c00199-sch-4-sec-33"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
